# Observability Provider Abstraction Rules

## Intent
Enable provider-neutral error monitoring so Sentry can be used now and Signoz can be adopted later with minimal refactoring.

## Mandatory
- All error capture must flow through the shared helper `reportError` in
  `ctf/packages/web/lib/observability/report.ts`. Today that helper is Sentry-specific behind the
  shared entry point: it calls `@sentry/nextjs` directly and falls back to stdout logging when
  Sentry is off. Only cron check-ins go through the provider-agnostic `ObservabilityReporter`
  interface (`lib/observability/types.ts`) with provider routing (sentry / noop).
- Feature modules must never call vendor SDKs directly — call `reportError` (errors) or the
  reporter interface (cron check-ins).
- Use normalized event shape (`message`, `level`, `tags`, `context`, `fingerprint`, `timestamp`).

## Migration Safety Rules
- Keep adapter contracts stable even if provider changes.
- Implement provider adapters in dedicated integration modules only.
- Preserve privacy scrubbing before provider handoff regardless of provider.

## Operational Rules
- Initialize provider once per runtime boundary.
- Fail open to no-op reporting if provider config is missing, while preserving local logging.
- Track provider health and dropped-event metrics.
- Use v3-specific DSNs/config and keep them isolated from legacy project telemetry.
- Configure by the environment variables the code actually reads:
	- Web: `OBSERVABILITY_PROVIDER` (`lib/observability/provider.ts`), `SENTRY_DSN` (server/edge),
	  `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` (browser bundle — introduced in PR #2074 because Next.js only inlines
	  `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables into the client), and `CTF_SKIP_SENTRY_NEXTJS` (set to `1` to skip
	  Sentry entirely, e.g. in CI builds).
	- Mobile: `MOBILE_OBSERVABILITY_PROVIDER` and `EXPO_SENTRY_DSN` are passed through by
	  `app.config.ts` but nothing consumes them yet — the mobile app has no observability
	  integration today.

## Prohibited
- Embedding provider-specific APIs into domain/business logic.
- Duplicating vendor-specific capture code across web and mobile features.
